diff --git a/proposals/window-open/README.md b/proposals/window-open/README.md
new file mode 100644
--- /dev/null
+++ b/proposals/window-open/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,30 @@
+This independently implemented bounded popup slice creates actual Page instances, VM contexts, Window globals and Documents in the same BrowserContext. Popup pages belong to the opener's existing CDP Page; they do not create extra Target entries or FrameTree children. The root registry finds their genuine frame/context IDs and routes actual execution, DOM, console, network and lifecycle observations through the opener session. Public handles are actual Window globals; there are no popup facades, proxies, fabricated messages or fake completion paths.
+
+Implemented measured behavior includes about:blank/default/empty URLs, inherited private origin/base/secure context, top-level self/window/top/parent identity, opener/null disowning, independent realms, actual document.open/write/close execution, named reuse and renaming, reserved target selection, noopener/noreferrer presence semantics including =0, real owned HTTP GET navigation/script execution/postMessage/self-close, script-close no-op on ordinary main/frame windows, and physical owner teardown. Script-close parks the real popup context and DOM; prior timers cancel and new timers still run. Closed contexts remain available to actual CDP Runtime evaluation until owner teardown, matching the measured retained lifetime.
+
+Production changes are one new popup-pages.js module, small Browser/Page initialization/teardown hooks, internal frame close calls routed through captured genuine cleanup functions, and one frame-activity context selection change. The latter uses the actual window's VM context during beforeParse, when a newly constructed Page's dom field has not yet been assigned. Existing adapter close chains perform real cleanup; popup script-close preserves the existing DOM tree and actual Window document slot, then clears the Document defaultView. Owner teardown aborts and physically closes every live or parked popup Page. Private Host WeakMaps track successful Window/Page initialization, opener, naming and popup lifetime. Authored objects, copied prototypes and Proxy receivers grant no open/close authority.
+
+Native binary SHA256: 9dec394124212f796724d4d32737ba66fdf0319ae6faaf8a1df8cccb4a70e23f. Source commit: 948d773786380bae36f046639fc61e2ddddd212a. window/open.html SHA256: feed197083de25079ac178cb07ca5b3b49ac9895f0422eb2da798dc442d1f012. popup_self_close.html SHA256: 1ec3034cc04a60e480defdb503faedd0744bc23ef77a3baca745a2c964aa1094. popup_idb_self_close.html SHA256: 1b8430a453ae84ad732c52ee7a17761999210e5c091141874ce3bcc4be73c046. Unmodified testing.js SHA256: 23e2ebbd851e64a68b1e357a38ed2e6d5d5f72217cb2e14671c4d3eecf6c861b.
+
+Native primary/extra reports contain 45 raw controls. Native navigation/tree reports retain complete original observations and event traces. Every report binds its expression/driver and executable by digest. Candidate raw rows are retained for each exact Node version. Test-only normalization replaces the independently allocated loopback origin; production values are unchanged. Actual helper drivers retain their original ../scripts and ../test relative imports: copy them/expressions into a direct repository child evidence directory when reproducing them.
+
+Validation: 7/7 focused popup acceptance tests pass serially on Node 24.19.0, 24.22.1 and 26.13.0 (acceptance-*.log). The final rebased Root graph also passed 45/45 popup plus frame/write/messaging tests on24.22 (final-24.22.1.log); later acceptance-only changes separated the known Document failure from popup acceptance without changing production. The unchanged window/open.html fixture passed on Native and candidate, including actual HTTP self-close. OwnedPopupOracle/1 user agent selects the harness's external-browser origin adaptation; __lp_external_runner=true keeps external polling ownership. This is explicitly the external harness branch, with unchanged assertions, nonzero observations and all module async blocks enforced by the real assertOk(). No canonical9582/9584 ports were used. Native canonical-profile results are not claimed by these ephemeral-port checks.
+
+Independent integration with immutable IndexedDB candidate-r1 (fake-indexeddb6.2.5 plus the agent's actual adapter) passed the full unchanged indexeddb.html, including popup_self_close: indexeddb-full51-final.json/log. Fixture SHA256: 6583e4ce6b8dc4a07f8a2fd506c62094f56874f52729dda654d94bce21ae15d7. combined-final-graph.json binds all 142 source files, native sources, actual runtime/version, backend dependency files and final report/stdout. The report includes captured child stderr. This combined graph includes current Root Payment/Crypto and the exact final popup production module. The dependency and IndexedDB leaves are separate ownership and are not added by this popup patch.
+
+Unresolved gaps are preserved, not normalized into success:
+
+* Native WindowProxy follows a new Window/VM/Document on navigation while retaining public handle identity. Current real Page.navigate creates a fresh genuine Window and retains the actual original Window/Document. Thus old handles keep their initial document/location and event.source is the new genuine Window. Native navigation.js and candidate-navigation-v2.json retain this mismatch. About:blank/no-navigation handle identity is genuine and matches.
+* The actual popup Window, script-created objects and Promises are created in the selected VM before and after prototype removal, verified by the real V8 creation-context API on all three runtimes (creation-*.json). The pinned generated Document wrapper is still Host-created, like the main Document. The original failed assertion/logs and separate deliberately failing document-creation-known-gap.mjs control plus raw failure report are retained. Popup acceptance does not convert that failure into a Host-allocation requirement. No prototype grafting or heap hints were used to force a realm result. Root's separate shared DOM allocation work owns this gap.
+* The existing Page/CDP adapter does not emit the entire Native scheduled/requested/cleared navigation event trace and retains its existing Page-domain gating. The implemented ownership, IDs, independent top-level frame membership, opener-session context events, execution and retirement are genuine; complete wire parity is not claimed.
+* Full cross-origin WindowProxy access checks, all non-null opener [Replaceable] descriptor details, exact named about:blank re-navigation/replacement behavior, complete history/target selection policy, nested popup/iframe edge cases, and all unmeasured coercion/teardown combinations remain incomplete. Existing generated DOM/Window platform allocation/brand gaps are inherited. Successful fixture runs do not establish full Lightpanda replication.
+
+The initial extra-v1 control intentionally/accidentally awaited after scheduling self-navigation and was interrupted by Native context destruction; the safe extra batch omits that pending navigation, while primary retains synchronous reserved-target observations. The first fixture driver sampled pending assertOk false too early; corrected reports poll for actual true. Original failures and early reports remain present. MaxListenersExceededWarning and VM Modules warnings remain visible.
+
+Run the bounded suite with each exact prepared Node executable:
