diff --git a/proposals/window-open/known-gaps.md b/proposals/window-open/known-gaps.md
new file mode 100644
--- /dev/null
+++ b/proposals/window-open/known-gaps.md
@@ -0,0 +1,5 @@
+The initial creation-realm assertion in candidate-second.log and candidate-third-regressions.log fails: the genuine existing jsdom Document wrapper reports Host creation context through the real V8 API, including after nulling their prototypes. The actual Window itself and independent VM script-created objects/Promises have the selected popup creation context. This is an existing foundation allocation gap, shared by the main Document, and has not been hidden by prototype changes or heap classification. creation.mjs records the unmodified before/after observations independently from matching controls.
+
+Native navigation.js has a stable WindowProxy: a popup handle follows the new document/VM, and e.source equals that handle. Candidate's normal Page.navigate creates a genuine fresh Window/VM/Document and preserves the actual initial Window/Document; its handle remains that original object. Therefore candidate-navigation-v2.json differs in source identity, original location/document/title. The raw Native and candidate results are retained. HTTP execution, opener messaging, close, frame context events and ownership are genuine; this checkpoint does not claim stable navigation WindowProxy behavior.
+
+The first extra-v1-destroyed.js awaited after scheduling _SELF navigation and the Native control was interrupted with CDP -32000 'Execution context was destroyed.' extra.js removes that context-destroying case from the async batch. primary.js retains synchronous _self/_parent/_top immediate observations. Fixture-probe-v1 reports sampled assertOk too early; corrected fixture-probe polls until actual true and keeps the originals.
